                            text "Development" 8 8855 100 19 serif 19 bold
                      block figure 48 8895 704 288
                        block anon 48 8895 704 268
                          line 48 8895 704 268 base 262
                            span a 48 9145 190 16 link 350
                            atomic img 48 8895 190 262 link 350
                        block figcaption 48 9163 704 20
                          line 48 9163 704 20 base 14
                            span a 48 9165 108 16 link 351
                            text "Tim Berners-Lee" 48 9165 108 16 serif 16 underline link 351
                            text " in April 2009" 156 9165 84 16 serif 16
                      block p 8 9199 784 120
                        line 8 9199 784 20 base 14
                          span a 88 9201 60 16 link 352
                          span a 152 9201 108 16 link 353
                          span a 364 9201 32 16 link 354
                          span a 568 9201 56 16 link 355
                          text "In 1980, the " 8 9201 80 16 serif 16
                          text "physicist" 88 9201 60 16 serif 16 underline link 352
                          text " " 148 9201 4 16 serif 16
                          text "Tim Berners-Lee" 152 9201 108 16 serif 16 underline link 353
                          text ", a contractor at " 260 9201 104 16 serif 16
                          text "CERN" 364 9201 32 16 serif 16 underline link 354
                          text ", proposed and prototyped " 396 9201 172 16 serif 16
                          text "ENQUIRE" 568 9201 56 16 serif 16 underline link 355
                          text ", a system for CERN" 624 9201 124 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9219 784 20 base 14
                          span a 604 9221 52 16 link 356
                          span a 708 9221 60 16 link 357
                          text "researchers to use and share documents. In 1989, Berners-Lee wrote a memo proposing an " 8 9221 596 16 serif 16
                          text "Internet" 604 9221 52 16 serif 16 underline link 356
                          text "-based " 656 9221 52 16 serif 16
                          text "hypertext" 708 9221 60 16 serif 16 underline link 357
                        line 8 9239 784 20 base 14
                          span span 60 9243 7 13
                          span span 73 9243 7 13
                          span span 60 9243 20 13
                          span a 60 9243 20 13 link 358
                          span sup 60 9243 20 13
                          text "system." 8 9241 52 16 serif 16
                          text "[" 60 9243 7 13 serif 13 underline link 358
                          text "4" 67 9243 6 13 serif 13 underline link 358
                          text "]" 73 9243 7 13 serif 13 underline link 358
                          text " Berners-Lee specified HTML and wrote the browser and server software in late 1990. That year, Berners-Lee" 80 9241 700 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9259 784 20 base 14
                          span a 72 9261 88 16 link 359
                          span a 224 9261 92 16 link 360
                          text "and CERN " 8 9261 64 16 serif 16
                          text "data systems" 72 9261 88 16 serif 16 underline link 359
                          text " engineer " 160 9261 64 16 serif 16
                          text "Robert Cailliau" 224 9261 92 16 serif 16 underline link 360
                          text " collaborated on a joint request for funding, but the project was not" 316 9261 428 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9279 784 20 base 14
                          text "formally adopted by CERN. In his personal notes of 1990, Berners-Lee listed \"some of the many areas in which hypertext" 8 9281 780 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9299 784 20 base 14
                          span a 92 9301 88 16 link 361
                          span span 288 9303 7 13
                          span span 301 9303 7 13
                          span span 288 9303 20 13
                          span a 288 9303 20 13 link 362
                          span sup 288 9303 20 13
                          text "is used\"; an " 8 9301 84 16 serif 16
                          text "encyclopedia" 92 9301 88 16 serif 16 underline link 361
                          text " is the first entry." 180 9301 108 16 serif 16
                          text "[" 288 9303 7 13 serif 13 underline link 362
                          text "5" 295 9303 6 13 serif 13 underline link 362
                          text "]" 301 9303 7 13 serif 13 underline link 362
                      block p 8 9335 784 80
                        line 8 9335 784 20 base 14
                          span span 564 9339 7 13
                          span span 577 9339 7 13
                          span span 564 9339 20 13
                          span a 564 9339 20 13 link 363
                          span sup 564 9339 20 13
                          text "The first publicly available description of HTML was a document called \"HTML Tags\"," 8 9337 556 16 serif 16
                          text "[" 564 9339 7 13 serif 13 underline link 363
                          text "6" 571 9339 6 13 serif 13 underline link 363
                          text "]" 577 9339 7 13 serif 13 underline link 363
                          text " first mentioned on the Internet" 584 9337 200 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9355 784 20 base 14
                          span span 212 9359 7 13
                          span span 225 9359 7 13
                          span span 212 9359 20 13
                          span a 212 9359 20 13 link 364
                          span sup 212 9359 20 13
                          span span 232 9359 6 13
                          span span 245 9359 6 13
                          span span 232 9359 19 13
                          span a 232 9359 19 13 link 365
                          span sup 232 9359 19 13
                          text "by Tim Berners-Lee in late 1991." 8 9357 204 16 serif 16
                          text "[" 212 9359 7 13 serif 13 underline link 364
                          text "7" 219 9359 6 13 serif 13 underline link 364
                          text "]" 225 9359 7 13 serif 13 underline link 364
                          text "[" 232 9359 6 13 serif 13 underline link 365
                          text "8" 238 9359 7 13 serif 13 underline link 365
                          text "]" 245 9359 6 13 serif 13 underline link 365
                          text " It describes 18 elements comprising the initial, relatively simple design of HTML." 251 9357 528 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9375 784 20 base 14
                          span a 416 9377 72 16 link 366
                          span a 580 9377 188 16 link 367
                          text "Except for the hyperlink tag, these were strongly influenced by " 8 9377 408 16 serif 16
                          text "CERN SGML" 416 9377 72 16 serif 16 underline link 366
                          text ", an in-house " 488 9377 92 16 serif 16
                          text "Standard Generalized Markup" 580 9377 188 16 serif 16 underline link 367
                        line 8 9395 784 20 base 14
                          span a 8 9397 64 16 link 367
                          span span 680 9399 7 13
                          span span 693 9399 7 13
                          span span 680 9399 20 13
                          span a 680 9399 20 13 link 368
                          span sup 680 9399 20 13
                          text "Language" 8 9397 64 16 serif 16 underline link 367
                          text " (SGML)-based documentation format at CERN. Eleven of these elements still exist in HTML 4." 72 9397 608 16 serif 16
                          text "[" 680 9399 7 13 serif 13 underline link 368
                          text "9" 687 9399 6 13 serif 13 underline link 368
                          text "]" 693 9399 7 13 serif 13 underline link 368
                      block p 8 9431 784 180
                        line 8 9431 784 20 base 14
                          span a 76 9433 112 16 link 369
                          span a 220 9433 92 16 link 370
                          span a 444 9433 60 16 link 371
                          text "HTML is a " 8 9433 68 16 serif 16
                          text "markup language" 76 9433 112 16 serif 16 underline link 369
                          text " that " 188 9433 32 16 serif 16
                          text "web browsers" 220 9433 92 16 serif 16 underline link 370
                          text " use to interpret and " 312 9433 132 16 serif 16
                          text "compose" 444 9433 60 16 serif 16 underline link 371
                          text " text, images, and other material into visible" 504 9433 284 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9451 784 20 base 14
                          text "or audible web pages. Default characteristics for every item of HTML markup are defined in the browser, and these" 8 9453 736 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9471 784 20 base 14
                          span a 584 9473 24 16 link 372
                          text "characteristics can be altered or enhanced by the web page designer's additional use of " 8 9473 576 16 serif 16
                          text "CSS" 584 9473 24 16 serif 16 underline link 372
                          text ". Many of the text elements" 608 9473 176 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9491 784 20 base 14
                          span i 364 9493 176 16
                          text "are mentioned in the 1988 ISO technical report TR 9537 " 8 9493 356 16 serif 16
                          text "Techniques for using SGML" 364 9493 176 16 serif 16 italic
                          text ", which describes the features of early" 540 9493 248 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9511 784 20 base 14
                          span a 340 9513 116 16 link 373
                          span a 692 9513 32 16 link 374
                          text "text formatting languages such as that used by the " 8 9513 332 16 serif 16
                          text "RUNOFF command" 340 9513 116 16 serif 16 underline link 373
                          text " developed in the early 1960s for the " 456 9513 236 16 serif 16
                          text "CTSS" 692 9513 32 16 serif 16 underline link 374
                        line 8 9531 784 20 base 14
                          text "(Compatible Time-Sharing System) operating system. These formatting commands were derived from the commands" 8 9533 760 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9551 784 20 base 14
                          text "used by typesetters to manually format documents. However, the SGML concept of generalized markup is based on" 8 9553 744 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9571 784 20 base 14
                          text "elements (nested annotated ranges with attributes) rather than merely print effects, with separate structure and markup." 8 9573 776 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9591 784 20 base 14
                          text "HTML has been progressively moved in this direction with CSS." 8 9593 408 16 serif 16
                      block p 8 9627 784 140
                        line 8 9627 784 20 base 14
                          span a 656 9629 132 16 link 375
                          text "Berners-Lee considered HTML to be an application of SGML. It was formally defined as such by the " 8 9629 648 16 serif 16
                          text "Internet Engineering" 656 9629 132 16 serif 16 underline link 375
                        line 8 9647 784 20 base 14
                          span a 8 9649 72 16 link 375
                          text "Task Force" 8 9649 72 16 serif 16 underline link 375
                          text " (IETF) with the mid-1993 publication of the first proposal for an HTML specification, the \"Hypertext Markup" 80 9649 696 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9667 784 20 base 14
                          span a 140 9669 84 16 link 376
                          span a 360 9669 84 16 link 377
                          span a 616 9669 160 16 link 378
                          text "Language (HTML)\" " 8 9669 132 16 serif 16
                          text "Internet Draft" 140 9669 84 16 serif 16 underline link 376
                          text " by Berners-Lee and " 224 9669 136 16 serif 16
                          text "Dan Connolly" 360 9669 84 16 serif 16 underline link 377
                          text ", which included an SGML " 444 9669 172 16 serif 16
                          text "document type definition" 616 9669 160 16 serif 16 underline link 378
                          text " to" 776 9669 16 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9687 784 20 base 14
                          span span 124 9691 7 13
                          span span 140 9691 7 13
                          span span 124 9691 23 13
                          span a 124 9691 23 13 link 379
                          span sup 124 9691 23 13
                          span span 147 9691 6 13
                          span span 160 9691 6 13
                          span span 147 9691 19 13
                          span a 147 9691 19 13 link 380
                          span sup 147 9691 19 13
                          span a 698 9689 84 16 link 381
                          text "define the syntax." 8 9689 116 16 serif 16
                          text "[" 124 9691 7 13 serif 13 underline link 379
                          text "10" 131 9691 9 13 serif 13 underline link 379
                          text "]" 140 9691 7 13 serif 13 underline link 379
                          text "[" 147 9691 6 13 serif 13 underline link 380
                          text "11" 153 9691 7 13 serif 13 underline link 380
                          text "]" 160 9691 6 13 serif 13 underline link 380
                          text " The draft expired after six months, but was notable for its acknowledgment of the " 166 9689 532 16 serif 16
                          text "NCSA Mosaic" 698 9689 84 16 serif 16 underline link 381
                        line 8 9707 784 20 base 14
                          text "browser's custom tag for embedding in-line images, reflecting the IETF's philosophy of basing standards on successful" 8 9709 780 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9727 784 20 base 14
                          span a 148 9729 84 16 link 382
                          text "prototypes. Similarly, " 8 9729 140 16 serif 16
                          text "Dave Raggett" 148 9729 84 16 serif 16 underline link 382
                          text "'s competing Internet Draft, \"HTML+ (Hypertext Markup Format)\", from late 1993," 232 9729 520 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9747 784 20 base 14
                          span span 560 9751 7 13
                          span span 576 9751 7 13
                          span span 560 9751 23 13
                          span a 560 9751 23 13 link 383
                          span sup 560 9751 23 13
                          text "suggested standardizing already-implemented features like tables and fill-out forms." 8 9749 552 16 serif 16
                          text "[" 560 9751 7 13 serif 13 underline link 383
                          text "12" 567 9751 9 13 serif 13 underline link 383
                          text "]" 576 9751 7 13 serif 13 underline link 383
                      block p 8 9783 784 60
                        line 8 9783 784 20 base 14
                          text "After the HTML and HTML+ drafts expired in early 1994, the IETF created an HTML Working Group. In 1995, this working" 8 9785 760 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9803 784 20 base 14
                          text "group completed \"HTML 2.0\", the first HTML specification intended to be treated as a standard against which future" 8 9805 744 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9823 784 20 base 14
                          span span 232 9827 7 13
                          span span 248 9827 7 13
                          span span 232 9827 23 13
                          span a 232 9827 23 13 link 384
                          span sup 232 9827 23 13
                          text "implementations should be based." 8 9825 224 16 serif 16
                          text "[" 232 9827 7 13 serif 13 underline link 384
                          text "13" 239 9827 9 13 serif 13 underline link 384
                          text "]" 248 9827 7 13 serif 13 underline link 384
                      block p 8 9859 784 120
                        line 8 9859 784 20 base 14
                          span span 584 9861 68 16
                          span span 652 9861 0 16
                          span span 652 9861 4 16
                          span span 656 9863 7 13
                          span span 698 9863 7 13
                          span a 656 9863 49 13 link 385
                          span sup 656 9863 49 13
                          span span 705 9861 0 16
                          text "Further development under the auspices of the IETF was stalled by competing interests. " 8 9861 576 16 serif 16
                          text "Since 1996" 584 9861 68 16 serif 16
                          text "," 652 9861 4 16 serif 16
                          text "[" 656 9863 7 13 serif 13 underline link 385
                          text "update" 663 9863 35 13 serif 13 underline link 385
                          text "]" 698 9863 7 13 serif 13 underline link 385
                          text " the HTML" 705 9861 64 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9879 784 20 base 14
                          span a 600 9881 180 16 link 386
                          text "specifications have been maintained, with input from commercial software vendors, by the " 8 9881 592 16 serif 16
                          text "World Wide Web Consortium" 600 9881 180 16 serif 16 underline link 386
                        line 8 9899 784 20 base 14
                          span span 56 9903 7 13
                          span span 72 9903 7 13
                          span span 56 9903 23 13
                          span a 56 9903 23 13 link 387
                          span sup 56 9903 23 13
                          span a 411 9901 24 16 link 388
                          span a 443 9901 24 16 link 389
                          text "(W3C)." 8 9901 48 16 serif 16
                          text "[" 56 9903 7 13 serif 13 underline link 387
                          text "14" 63 9903 9 13 serif 13 underline link 387
                          text "]" 72 9903 7 13 serif 13 underline link 387
                          text " In 2000, HTML became an international standard (" 79 9901 332 16 serif 16
                          text "ISO" 411 9901 24 16 serif 16 underline link 388
                          text "/" 435 9901 8 16 serif 16
                          text "IEC" 443 9901 24 16 serif 16 underline link 389
                          text " 15445:2000). HTML 4.01 was published in late" 467 9901 300 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9919 784 20 base 14
                          span a 616 9921 168 16 link 390
                          text "1999, with further errata published through 2001. In 2004, development began on HTML5 in the " 8 9921 608 16 serif 16
                          text "Web Hypertext Application" 616 9921 168 16 serif 16 underline link 390
                        line 8 9939 784 20 base 14
                          span a 8 9941 172 16 link 390
                          text "Technology Working Group" 8 9941 172 16 serif 16 underline link 390
                          text " (WHATWG), which became a joint deliverable with the W3C in 2008, and was completed and" 180 9941 604 16 serif 16
                        line 8 9959 784 20 base 14
                          span span 220 9963 7 13
                          span span 236 9963 7 13
                          span span 220 9963 23 13
                          span a 220 9963 23 13 link 391
                          span sup 220 9963 23 13
                          text "standardized on 28 October 2014." 8 9961 212 16 serif 16
                          text "[" 220 9963 7 13 serif 13 underline link 391
                          text "15" 227 9963 9 13 serif 13 underline link 391
                          text "]" 236 9963 7 13 serif 13 underline link 391
