                          line 48 12328 744 20 base 14
                            span a 224 12330 28 16 link 477
                            text "In July 2012, WHATWG and " 48 12330 176 16 serif 16
                            text "W3C" 224 12330 28 16 serif 16 underline link 477
                            text " decided on a degree of separation. W3C will continue the HTML5 specification" 252 12330 508 16 serif 16
                          line 48 12348 744 20 base 14
                            text "work, focusing on a single definitive standard, which is considered a \"snapshot\" by WHATWG. The WHATWG" 48 12350 700 16 serif 16
                          line 48 12368 744 20 base 14
                            text "organization will continue its work with HTML5 as a \"Living Standard\". The concept of a living standard is that it is" 48 12370 744 16 serif 16
                          line 48 12388 744 20 base 14
                            text "never complete and is always being updated and improved. New features can be added but functionality will not" 48 12390 728 16 serif 16
                          line 48 12408 744 20 base 14
                            span span 128 12412 7 13
                            span span 148 12412 6 13
                            span span 128 12412 26 13
                            span a 128 12412 26 13 link 478
