                      block p 8 22752 784 40
                        line 8 22752 784 20 base 14
                          span code 556 22754 64 16
                          text "The Frameset version includes everything in the Transitional version, as well as the " 8 22754 548 16 serif 16
                          text "frameset" 556 22754 64 16 mono 16
                          text " element (used instead of" 620 22754 168 16 serif 16
                        line 8 22772 784 20 base 14
                          span code 8 22774 32 16
                          span code 104 22774 40 16
                          text "body" 8 22774 32 16 mono 16
                          text ") and the " 40 22774 64 16 serif 16
                          text "frame" 104 22774 40 16 mono 16
                          text " element." 144 22774 60 16 serif 16
                    block section 8 22811 784 102
                      block div 8 22811 784 23
                        block h3 8 22811 784 23
                          line 8 22811 784 23 base 16
                            text "Frameset versus transitional" 8 22813 219 19 serif 19 bold
                      block p 8 22853 784 60
                        line 8 22853 784 20 base 14
                          text "In addition to the above transitional differences, the frameset specifications (whether XHTML 1.0 or HTML 4.01) specify a" 8 22855 780 16 serif 16
                        line 8 22873 784 20 base 14
                          span code 196 22875 64 16
                          span code 328 22875 32 16
                          span code 496 22875 40 16
                          span code 692 22875 64 16
                          text "different content model, with " 8 22875 188 16 serif 16
                          text "frameset" 196 22875 64 16 mono 16
                          text " replacing " 260 22875 68 16 serif 16
                          text "body" 328 22875 32 16 mono 16
                          text ", that contains either " 360 22875 136 16 serif 16
                          text "frame" 496 22875 40 16 mono 16
                          text " elements, or optionally " 536 22875 156 16 serif 16
                          text "noframes" 692 22875 64 16 mono 16
                          text " with" 756 22875 32 16 serif 16
                        line 8 22893 784 20 base 14
                          span code 20 22895 32 16
                          text "a " 8 22895 12 16 serif 16
                          text "body" 20 22895 32 16 mono 16
                          text "." 52 22895 4 16 serif 16
                    block section 8 22932 784 358
                      block div 8 22932 784 24
                        block h3 8 22932 784 24
                          line 8 22932 784 24 base 16
                            text "Summary of specification versions" 8 22934 266 19 serif 19 bold
                      block p 8 22974 784 200
                        line 8 22974 784 20 base 14
                          text "As this list demonstrates, the loose versions of the specification are maintained for legacy support. However, contrary to" 8 22976 776 16 serif 16
                        line 8 22994 784 20 base 14
                          text "popular misconceptions, the move to XHTML does not imply a removal of this legacy support. Rather the X in XML stands" 8 22996 780 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23014 784 20 base 14
                          text "for extensible and the W3C is modularizing the entire specification and opens it up to independent extensions. The" 8 23016 740 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23034 784 20 base 14
                          text "primary achievement in the move from XHTML 1.0 to XHTML 1.1 is the modularization of the entire specification. The strict" 8 23036 772 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23054 784 20 base 14
                          text "version of HTML is deployed in XHTML 1.1 through a set of modular extensions to the base XHTML 1.1 specification." 8 23056 732 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23074 784 20 base 14
                          text "Likewise, someone looking for the loose (transitional) or frameset specifications will find similar extended XHTML 1.1" 8 23076 760 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23094 784 20 base 14
                          text "support (much of it is contained in the legacy or frame modules). Modularization also allows for separate features to" 8 23096 756 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23114 784 20 base 14
                          text "develop on their own timetable. So for example, XHTML 1.1 will allow quicker migration to emerging XML standards such" 8 23116 772 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23134 784 20 base 14
                          span a 28 23136 52 16 link 647
                          span a 524 23136 48 16 link 648
                          text "as " 8 23136 20 16 serif 16
                          text "MathML" 28 23136 52 16 serif 16 underline link 647
                          text " (a presentational and semantic math language based on XML) and " 80 23136 444 16 serif 16
                          text "XForms" 524 23136 48 16 serif 16 underline link 648
                          text "—a new highly advanced" 572 23136 160 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23154 784 20 base 14
                          text "web-form technology to replace the existing HTML forms." 8 23156 372 16 serif 16
                      block p 8 23190 784 100
                        line 8 23190 784 20 base 14
                          text "In summary, the HTML 4 specification primarily reined in all the various HTML implementations into a single clearly" 8 23192 748 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23210 784 20 base 14
                          text "written specification based on SGML. XHTML 1.0, ported this specification, as is, to the new XML-defined specification." 8 23212 768 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23230 784 20 base 14
                          text "Next, XHTML 1.1 takes advantage of the extensible nature of XML and modularizes the whole specification. XHTML 2.0" 8 23232 756 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23250 784 20 base 14
                          text "was intended to be the first step in adding new features to the specification in a standards-body-based" 8 23252 672 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23270 784 20 base 14
                          span span 72 23275 7 13
                          span span 79 23275 78 13
                          span span 79 23275 78 13
                          span a 79 23275 78 13 link 649
                          span i 79 23275 78 13
                          span span 157 23275 6 13
                          span sup 72 23275 91 13
                          text "approach." 8 23272 64 16 serif 16
                          text "[" 72 23275 7 13 serif 13
                          text "AI-generated?" 79 23275 78 13 serif 13 italic underline link 649
                          text "]" 157 23275 6 13 serif 13
                  block section 8 23310 784 126
                    block div 8 23310 784 30
                      block h2 8 23310 784 30
                        line 8 23310 784 30 base 21
                          text "WHATWG HTML versus HTML5" 8 23313 288 24 serif 24 bold
                    block div 8 23360 784 20
                      line 8 23360 784 20 base 14
                        span span 140 23362 8 16
                        span a 92 23362 328 16 link 650
                        text "Main article: " 8 23362 84 16 serif 16
                        text "HTML §" 92 23362 48 16 serif 16 underline link 650
                        text " " 140 23362 8 16 serif 16 underline link 650
                        text "Transition of HTML publication to WHATWG" 148 23362 272 16 serif 16 underline link 650
                    block p 8 23396 784 40
                      line 8 23396 784 20 base 14
                        text "The HTML Living Standard, which is developed by WHATWG, is the official version, while W3C HTML5 is no longer" 8 23398 732 16 serif 16
                      line 8 23416 784 20 base 14
                        text "separate from WHATWG." 8 23418 152 16 serif 16
                  block section 8 23456 784 466
                    block div 8 23456 784 30
                      block h2 8 23456 784 30
